<http://weee-kg.org/source:A%20Copper-Catalyzed%20Bioleaching%20Process%20for%20Enhancement%20of%20Cobalt%20Dissolution%20from%20Spent%20Lithium-Ion%20Batteries:Observation_REL_reviewed_ca2b9ad47a5b8ec4_9025c432312a2005> a weee:Observation ;
    rdfs:label "dissolution: 32.7 % for Co under copper ion 10 g/L" ;
    weee:conditionLabel "copper ion 10 g/L" ;
    weee:description "A. ferrooxidans bioleaching with 10 g/L copper ion has a dissolution observation for Co as 32.7 %. Source study: A Copper-Catalyzed Bioleaching Process for Enhancement of Cobalt Dissolution from Spent Lithium-Ion Batteries. Conditions: copper ion 10 g/L." ;
    weee:evidenceSpan "when the copper ions concentrations were 0.01, 0.1 and 10 g/L, cobalt dissolution percentages were 46.0%, 86.4% and 32.7%, respectively" ;
    weee:observationProperty "dissolution" ;
    weee:observationUnit "%" ;
    weee:observationValue 32.7 ;
    weee:originalRelationType "HAS_OUTPUT" ;
    weee:settingCondition "copper ion 10 g/L" ;
    weee:sourceEntityEvidence "The dissolution percentages of cobalt catalyzed under different Cu ^2+ concentrations are shown in Fig. 3, which show that copper ion has an important catalytic effect on the dissolution rate and cobalt dissolution percentage. The best catalytic effect was obtained using 0.75 g copper/L at 6 days, cobalt dissolution percentage increased from 43.1% in the absence of copper ions to 99.9% at the copper concentration of 0.75 g / L, and the corresponding Co concentration was 4.8 g/L. However, when the copper ions concentrations were 0.01, 0.1 and 10 g/L, cobalt dissolution percentages were 46.0%, 86.4% and 32.7%, respectively. It shows that additional amounts of Cu ^2+ increased the percentage of leached cobalt, which is in agreement with the previous study. Ballester et al. [18] reported that the microbiological dissolution ofthe sphalerite improves considerably when using Ag ^+ and Cu ^2+ as catalysts, with zinc dissolution of 90%. Furthermore, it showed that additional amounts of Cu ^2+ increased the percentage of metal leached." ;
    weee:sourcePaper "A Copper-Catalyzed Bioleaching Process for Enhancement of Cobalt Dissolution from Spent Lithium-Ion Batteries" ;
    weee:sourceRelationId "REL_reviewed_ca2b9ad47a5b8ec4" ;
    weee:sourceSample "spent lithium-ion batteries" ;
    rel:observedMaterial <http://weee-kg.org/entity/Co> .

<http://weee-kg.org/source:A%20Copper-Catalyzed%20Bioleaching%20Process%20for%20Enhancement%20of%20Cobalt%20Dissolution%20from%20Spent%20Lithium-Ion%20Batteries:Process_reviewed_5a8f38ab000de8> a weee:Process ;
    rdfs:label "A. ferrooxidans bioleaching with 10 g/L copper ion" ;
    weee:description "A. ferrooxidans bioleaching with 10 g/L copper ion is a source-specific Process entity in the study A Copper-Catalyzed Bioleaching Process for Enhancement of Cobalt Dissolution from Spent Lithium-Ion Batteries. Quantitative observations concern: Co." ;
