<http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/1dca63a76aa7242b176f1510> a weee:ScopeContext ;
    weee:bindingStatus "bound" ;
    weee:description "Crushed lithium iron phosphate power battery core products (copper and aluminum foil current collectors with particle sizes 3–15 mm, dissociated electrode powders) are fed into a pneumatic separation system where airflow velocity and inclination angle separate materials based on aerodynamic drag and gravity; the process is modeled with horizontal and vertical motion equations accounting for drag force, buoyancy, additional mass force, Saffman lift, Basset force, Magnus force, and pressure gradient force, with particle-wall and particle-particle interactions neglected." ;
    weee:evidenceRef "scope:scope-assertion:fac85d658ee43dea:evidence",
        "source:Pneumatic Separation and Recycling of Anode and Cathode Materials from Spent Lithium Iron Phosphate Batteries:Process_pneumatic_separation_of_crushed_battery_core_product:entity" ;
    weee:evidenceSpan "Crushed lithium iron phosphate power battery core products (copper and aluminum foil current collectors with particle sizes 3–15 mm, dissociated electrode powders) are fed into a pneumatic separation system where airflow velocity and inclination angle separate materials based on aerodynamic drag and gravity; the process is modeled with horizontal and vertical motion equations accounting for drag force, buoyancy, additional mass force, Saffman lift, Basset force, Magnus force, and pressure gradient force, with particle-wall and particle-particle interactions neglected." ;
    weee:methodFamily "pneumatic separation" ;
    weee:micrographId "Pneumatic Separation and Recycling of Anode and Cathode Materials from Spent Lithium Iron Phosphate Batteries" ;
    weee:scopeDescription "Crushed lithium iron phosphate power battery core products (copper and aluminum foil current collectors with particle sizes 3–15 mm, dissociated electrode powders) are fed into a pneumatic separation system where airflow velocity and inclination angle separate materials based on aerodynamic drag and gravity; the process is modeled with horizontal and vertical motion equations accounting for drag force, buoyancy, additional mass force, Saffman lift, Basset force, Magnus force, and pressure gradient force, with particle-wall and particle-particle interactions neglected." ;
    weee:scopeFacetsJson "{\"method_family\": \"pneumatic separation\"}" ;
    weee:scopeId "scope-assertion:fac85d658ee43dea" ;
    weee:scopeKind "process_method_family" ;
    weee:sourcePaper "Pneumatic Separation and Recycling of Anode and Cathode Materials from Spent Lithium Iron Phosphate Batteries" .

