<http://weee-kg.org/source:Heat%20Treatment%20of%20Licoo2%20Recovered%20from%20Cathode%20Scraps%20with%20Solvent%20Method:Process_electrochemical_cycling_of_recovered_scrap_material_electrodes> a weee:Process ;
    rdfs:label "electrochemical cycling of recovered scrap material electrodes" ;
    weee:description "electrochemical cycling of recovered scrap material electrodes is a source-specific Process entity in the study Heat Treatment of Licoo2 Recovered from Cathode Scraps with Solvent Method. Scope: Cathode electrodes were fabricated with 83 wt.% active materials (from recovered scrap materials), 10 wt.% acetylene black, and 7 wt.% PVDF in NMP; CR2032 coin cells with lithium foil anode and 1 M LiPF6 in EC:DEC (1:1 v/v) were charged/discharged between 3.0 V and 4.3 V vs Li+/Li at 30 mA g-1 and 25 °C." ;
    weee:hasScopeContext <http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/0f0086b176316e79a2329105> ;
    rel:hasOutput <http://weee-kg.org/entity/LiCoO2> ;
    rel:memberOfMethodFamily <http://weee-kg.org/anchor:MethodFamily:electrochemical_cycling> .

