    rdfs:label "electrode material" ;
    weee:description "electrode material is a source-specific Component entity in the study Pyrolysis-Ultrasonic-Assisted Flotation Technology for Recovering Graphite and Licoosub2sub from Spent Lithium-Ion Batteries. Scope: Electrode materials obtained by combining crushing and sieving, with a 0.075 mm size screen hole used to obtain fine-sized electrode materials; separated by filtration and dried at 80 °C. Directly contains: LiCoO2, PVDF, dimethyl carbonate, electrolyte, ethylene carbonate." ;
    weee:hasScopeContext <http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/da20ff77f106c89c570745f5> ;
    rel:comparableSamplePopulation <http://weee-kg.org/source:Synthesis%20and%20Performance%20of%20Li%5B%28ni13co13mn13%291%E2%88%92mg%20%5Do2%20Prepared%20from%20Spent%20Lithium%20Ion%20Batteries:Component_cathode>,
