<http://weee-kg.org/source:Bioleaching%20of%20Valuable%20Metals%20from%20Spent%20Lithium-Ion%20Mobile%20Phone%20Batteries%20Using%20Aspergillus%20Niger:Process_chemical_leaching> a weee:Process ;
    rdfs:label "chemical leaching" ;
    weee:description "chemical leaching is a source-specific Process entity in the study Bioleaching of Valuable Metals from Spent Lithium-Ion Mobile Phone Batteries Using Aspergillus Niger. Scope: Spent battery powder (1% w/v) was leached in 100 mL of a mixture of commercial citric acid, oxalic acid, malic acid, and gluconic acid at concentrations similar to those in bioleaching, in a 250 mL Erlenmeyer flask shaken at 130 rpm and 30 °C." ;
    weee:hasScopeContext <http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/e278cfb335bddf547df182d0> ;
    rel:memberOfMethodFamily <http://weee-kg.org/anchor:MethodFamily:chemical_leaching> .

